tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-2308-a-quoted-use-is-advised-a-line-the-compiler-reads.hero:12:5: error[use_holds_an_address]: `github.com/acme/toml` is an address, which the catalogue `heroes.toml` beside the file you compile holds and a `use` never does: the `use` names its entry between `<` `>`, then a module of the package — `use <toml>/parse`, `toml` standing for the entry the catalogue gives that address and `parse` for one of the package's modules
tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-2308-a-quoted-use-is-advised-a-line-the-compiler-reads.hero:13:5: error[use_holds_an_address]: `github.com/acme/toml` is an address, which the catalogue `heroes.toml` beside the file you compile holds and a `use` never does: the `use` names its entry between `<` `>`, then a module of the package — `use <toml>/read`, `toml` standing for the entry the catalogue gives that address
tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-2308-a-quoted-use-is-advised-a-line-the-compiler-reads.hero:14:5: error[use_wants_a_name]: a module is named, not quoted, and `my-lib` is no module's name: each part of a `use` path is a name, letters, digits and `_` not opening with a digit and no word of the language, so a file named otherwise is one no `use` reaches
tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-2308-a-quoted-use-is-advised-a-line-the-compiler-reads.hero:15:5: error[use_wants_a_name]: a module is named, not quoted, and these quotes hold nothing — `use geom` reads `geom.hero` from the directory of the file you compile
